WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:13.750
I am Braden Hamilton,

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.480
and I am the founder of
Orca Asphalt Maintenance.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.950
One of our primary services
is asphalt seal coating.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.751
I'm going to walk you
through how we clean,

00:00:22.751 --> 00:00:26.498
repair, and seal an asphalt driveway.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.150
So, typically when we
show up on a project,

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.600
we assess the driveway, and we see cracks.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.100
Now, cracks are inevitable.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.900
Over time, asphalt moves,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.451
and typically what we see

00:00:40.451 --> 00:00:42.260
is cracks down the seams of the asphalt,

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.990
which could be in the
center of the driveway

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.010
or where the driveway meets the road.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.295
So, before we start our
seal-coating project,

00:00:48.295 --> 00:00:50.317
there is a lot of dirt and debris,

00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:52.450
grime, oils that need to be cleaned off.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.930
The reason for this is we want our sealer

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.480
to properly adhere to the asphalt.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.300
After the driveway is cleaned,

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.008
we then use an oil spot primer

00:01:03.008 --> 00:01:05.066
on any spots where oil has been leaked

00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:07.160
from out of cars or motorcycles.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.472
This oil spot primer is poured on the spot

00:01:09.472 --> 00:01:12.120
and then applied with
a broom to work it in.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.402
This ensures that the oil
doesn't penetrate through

00:01:15.402 --> 00:01:19.039
and that our sealer is able
to stick on that surface.

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:21.340
Crack sealing is an essential
part of the process,

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.991
as it prevents water from
penetrating into the asphalt.

00:01:24.991 --> 00:01:26.800
That water can wash away the base,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.620
which will eventually
lead to asphalt failure.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.891
The asphalt on top can cave in,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.374
and potholes can form,

00:01:33.374 --> 00:01:35.707
and much worse issues can arise.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.128
We begin the repair

00:01:38.128 --> 00:01:40.510
by ensuring that crack is perfectly clean,

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:43.800
and then we use our push-behind melters,

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.835
which melt a rubber compound.

00:01:45.835 --> 00:01:47.434
It comes out of the machine

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.784
through a spout and into the shoe,

00:01:49.784 --> 00:01:51.742
which is then walked along the crack,

00:01:51.742 --> 00:01:53.270
filling the void.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.528
This rubber compound is formulated

00:01:55.528 --> 00:01:57.228
to expand and contract

00:01:57.228 --> 00:02:00.062
with the thermal expansion of the asphalt.

00:02:00.062 --> 00:02:01.854
Typically one pass is needed,

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:03.478
but if that crack is large,

00:02:03.478 --> 00:02:05.880
we need to go over top of
that crack several times

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.680
to ensure it's properly sealed.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:10.450
In the winter months,

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.890
the asphalt will contract,

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.450
leaving a larger void in that asphalt.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.383
And in the summer, it expands,

00:02:17.383 --> 00:02:18.966
leaving the cracks smaller.

00:02:18.966 --> 00:02:21.158
We want a compound that can get in there

00:02:21.158 --> 00:02:23.750
and expand and contract with that crack,

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.430
ensuring that it doesn't open up

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.032
and further moisture can penetrate.

00:02:28.032 --> 00:02:29.031
The push-behind melter

00:02:29.031 --> 00:02:31.706
is heated to 350 degrees Celsius,

00:02:31.706 --> 00:02:33.620
which is the perfect
temperature for the rubber

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.880
to come out of the
machine and fill the crack

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.630
at a perfect consistency.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:42.160
Now that we're done repairing the cracks,

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:42.993
we're going to move on

00:02:42.993 --> 00:02:45.165
to seal coating the driveway.

00:02:46.156 --> 00:02:48.189
Seal coating protects from salt,

00:02:48.189 --> 00:02:50.313
UV rays, water penetration,

00:02:50.313 --> 00:02:51.792
and many other contaminants.

00:02:51.792 --> 00:02:55.580
We use a professional-grade
asphalt emulsion sealer

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.327
that has compounds that ensure

00:02:57.327 --> 00:03:00.700
that it's durable and nonslip.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.150
So in a residential setting,

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.006
we use specialized seal-coating brooms.

00:03:05.006 --> 00:03:07.090
So the product is applied in lines,

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.370
and then we come behind with brooms,

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.080
sweeping it back and forth,

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.074
working that sealer
into the asphalt pores.

00:03:15.007 --> 00:03:17.390
Seal coating a driveway is
a little bit like a dance.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:20.240
So we've got typically
two people on a project,

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.270
and we are working it back and forth,

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:25.124
pulling it down on the
edges, working our edges,

00:03:25.124 --> 00:03:27.600
and then working the
middle all at the same time

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.151
so that it cures in beautifully.

00:03:30.151 --> 00:03:32.060
So, our sealer is housed in a tank.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.700
We have a pump that
pumps it out of the tank,

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.240
through a hose, and out of a wand.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:39.476
Through this wand comes the sealer,

00:03:39.476 --> 00:03:41.660
and it is applied in lines.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.920
And then we come behind with brooms,

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.787
and we work that sealer back and forth,

00:03:46.787 --> 00:03:47.620
back and forth,

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.028
working it into the pores

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.028
and leaving a perfect finish.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.430
So, when the sealer is applied,

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.746
it has a brown color,

00:03:54.746 --> 00:03:56.880
and it cures to a jet black.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.197
We chalk-line a perfect line

00:03:58.197 --> 00:03:59.847
at the end of the driveways,

00:03:59.847 --> 00:04:01.260
and then we mask it off,

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.910
so that when we pull the sealer

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.559
onto the masking paper

00:04:04.559 --> 00:04:06.048
and pull it up at the end,

00:04:06.048 --> 00:04:08.498
customers are left with a perfect line.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.150
It will typically take
between three and four hours

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.900
to walk on the driveway,

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.466
but we always recommend 24 to 48 hours

00:04:16.466 --> 00:04:18.533
prior to driving.

00:04:18.533 --> 00:04:20.490
We recommend that
driveways are seal coated

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.390
every three to four years.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.440
We recommend getting this process done

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.606
in the summer months, as the temperatures

00:04:26.606 --> 00:04:29.903
allow it to cure properly and fast.

